EPrime's Readouts replaces the vanilla resource readout with customizable display groups. No setup required, safe to add or remove from saves.

Design your own groups of resources, arrange each group in up to three display tiers, and cycle how much detail a group shows with a click. Groups render as compact bands with a colored stripe and translucent backing so counters stay readable against the map.

[h1]Key Features[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Display groups:[/b] Each group is a band of resource icons with counters. Groups can be enabled/disabled and reordered.
[*] [b]Tiers:[/b] Put your must-see resources in tier 1 and details in tiers 2-3. Click a band's triangle markers to cycle how many tiers are shown.
[*] [b]Resource pools:[/b] One slot can show a whole category - all meats, all leathers, all stone blocks - as a single icon with the summed count.
[*] [b]Beyond resources:[/b] Any storable item can be tracked, not just resources - weapons, apparel, bionics and more can be added to groups and pools.
[*] [b]Material debt:[/b] Options to deduct materials needed for planned work (bills, buildables). Supports [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3776722051]EPrime's Quality Jobs[/url].
[*] [b]Sensible defaults:[/b] Seeded groups (Food, Raw, Medicine, Drugs, Textiles, Materials, Wealth) cover every vanilla and DLC resource. A Restore Defaults button brings them back anytime.
[*] [b]Quick search:[/b] Type to highlight matches and list every matching resource on the map, including ones not in any group. Can be configured or turned off in options.
[*] [b]Thresholds:[/b] Set low/critical levels per resource; counters tint yellow/orange and thresholded resources stay visible at zero.
[*] [b]Show when zero:[/b] Per-slot control over whether a resource shows at zero count.
[*] [b]Drag-and-drop editor:[/b] A config dialog with a live per-tier preview that renders exactly like the readout does in-game.
[*] [b]Import/Export:[/b] Easily share or back up your readout setup.
[*] [b]No camera fights:[/b] Hovering the readout suppresses screen-edge scrolling, so clicking near the left edge never drifts the map.
[*] [b]Designed for Performance:[/b] Extensive caching, rendering from pre-calculated caches, scoped invalidation, no per-tick logic.
[*] [b]Multiplayer:[/b] Fully [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2606448745]RimWorld Multiplayer[/url] compatible - group definitions are shared and synced; what each player shows is their own choice.
[/list]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
[list]
[*] Save compatible: add or remove at any time. Removing a content mod cleans its resources from your groups automatically.
[*] MultiFloors supported: readouts show combined resource counts across all floors of a level stack. Other multi-floor mods (Strata, 'As above, so below 2') work without needing special support.
[*] Not compatible with other mods that replace the resource readout (Readouts+, Custom Resource Readout, Toggleable Readouts, and similar).
[*] Requires Harmony.
[/list]

Found a bug or an incompatible mod? Let me know in the comments.

